From e6fd834d7367ea0abad03fcfe513653ccb0e17c6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michael Spanier <spanier.michael@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 22:56:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 16/43] acpi: zero the EC cookie allocated from the ECDT

embedded_controller_probe_ecdt() allocated the cookie with malloc()
and set only some fields; init_driver() clears its cookie with
memset(). With a kernel heap that fills new blocks with 0xcc
(KDEBUG_LEVEL 2), ec_sci_pending started at 0xcccccccc, so
EcGpeHandler() never queued a query: no _Qxx method ran and no
Notify reached the lid, AC adapter or battery devices.

Use calloc() like the other path does.

Tested on a ThinkPad T470s, which has an ECDT: lid and AC adapter
changes now reach acpi_lid and acpi_ac within a second, the SCI
rate dropped from about 380/s to about 35/s, and the lid handling
of the power_daemon from #530 works.

Signed-off-by: Michael Spanier <spanier.michael@gmail.com>
Assisted-by: claude-opus-5-5
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FZxbWGYWmZfrWCoDt1wNjX
(cherry picked from commit 8cea83936a86e0b4100c9870b4f6e54c8c61da6b)
---
 src/add-ons/kernel/bus_managers/acpi/EmbeddedController.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/add-ons/kernel/bus_managers/acpi/EmbeddedController.cpp b/src/add-ons/kernel/bus_managers/acpi/EmbeddedController.cpp
index 9377e81f13..f72d748409 100644
--- a/src/add-ons/kernel/bus_managers/acpi/EmbeddedController.cpp
+++ b/src/add-ons/kernel/bus_managers/acpi/EmbeddedController.cpp
@@ -343,7 +343,7 @@ embedded_controller_probe_ecdt()
 	if (ACPI_FAILURE(status))
 		return;
 
-	acpi_ec_cookie* sc = (acpi_ec_cookie*)malloc(sizeof(acpi_ec_cookie));
+	acpi_ec_cookie* sc = (acpi_ec_cookie*)calloc(1, sizeof(acpi_ec_cookie));
 	if (sc == NULL)
 		return;
 
